V4 -- THE VERDICTS
==================================================================================================
  V1 (the measured inner slopes with their errors):  median = -1.53 +- 0.25 (between-cluster scatter), SE(median) = 0.074, mean MC error = 0.28; per cluster: A1644 -1.35+-0.40, A1795 -1.87+-0.14, A2029 -1.70+-0.21, A2142 -1.55+-0.22, A2255 -1.26+-0.35, A2319 -1.84+-0.40, A3158 -1.50+-0.23, A3266 -2.18+-0.33, A644 -1.41+-0.28, A85 -1.66+-0.14, RXC1825 -1.50+-0.26, ZW1215 -1.35+-0.28
  V2 (the outcome): ~-1.5 (the theory's value), with the measured median sitting on the registered -1.5 (-0.4 sigma); the flat NFW cusp (-1) and the isothermal r^-2 (-2) are both excluded (>6 sigma); NFW-as-a-model is NOT excluded because over this window its own committed fits predict -1.66 -- the -1-vs-1.5 distinction is undecided at this resolution in the precise sense stated in V3
  V3 (the D2 statement): THE D2 FALSIFIER (H012): NOT TRIGGERED ON THE COMMITTED X-COP DATA -- the measured inner residual slope over 0.1-0.5 R500 is -1.53 (median, 12 clusters, scatter 0.25), inconsistent with the kill line -1 at 7.2 sigma and consistent with the theory's registered ~-1.5 at 0.4 sigma; the isothermal r^-2 (the law's one-component profile) is excluded at 6.4 sigma, so the two-component composite (phantom + dust) is required, exactly as H012 constructed it.  THE HONEST CAP: the flat-cusp -1 is only realized for r << rs; the committed NFW fits (median rs = 0.48 R500) predict s = -1.68 over THIS window, only 1.7 sigma from the measurement -- so D2 as registered (NFW -1 vs theory -1.5) is UNDECIDED at this resolution in the decisive direction: both pictures reproduce -1.5 to -1.7 over 0.1-0.5 R500 and both steepen outward.  WHAT RESOLVES IT: the core below ~0.1 R500 (20-70 kpc here) -- lensing inner mass profiles (HST/Subaru strong+weak lensing) that are free of the hydrostatic assumption, or XRISM-class temperature deprojection with non-thermal-pressure corrections; at such radii NFW turns toward -1 while the theory's composite stays ~-1.5.  Until then, the X-COP inner slope stands as a PASS for the theory's registered number (-0.4 sigma) and as a NON-DECISION against NFW.
